---
import { buildRevision } from "../build";

const pinned = /^[a-f0-9]{40}$/.test(buildRevision);
const command = `git clone https://github.com/bayleafwalker/kotona.app.git kotona-case
git -C kotona-case checkout --detach ${buildRevision}
git clone https://github.com/bayleafwalker/acceptance-lab.git acceptance-lab-case
git -C acceptance-lab-case checkout --detach fddbab2e26398f0ecddfc89cd291462effdc8e75
cd kotona-case
node --test tests/acceptance-case.test.mjs
python3 docs/experiments/2026-11-20-acceptance-case/run_case.py replay \\
  --case-dir public/evidence/acceptance-lab/2026-11-20-campaign-provenance \\
  --lab ../acceptance-lab-case --site . \\
  --out "$(mktemp -d)/replay"`;
---

<section aria-label="Reproduce the retained Acceptance Lab case">
  <p>
    Use Python 3.12 or newer, Node 24, and Git. These commands verify the
    retained bytes and re-evaluate the recorded answer; they do not call a model
    or repeat the original agent session. Neither repository needs package
    installation.
  </p>
  {
    pinned ? (
      <>
        <p>
          Site source: <code class="source-revision">{buildRevision}</code>. The
          Lab revision is fixed separately below. Use new destination
          directories.
        </p>
        <pre>
          <code>{command}</code>
        </pre>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        This preview has no pinned source revision. The published page supplies
        the complete checkout command once its source commit is known.
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    Expected: four integrity tests pass; the observed case is <code
      >CONDITIONAL</code
    >
    because billing is unknown; all three constructed controls are <code
      >FAIL</code
    >
    after source verification. The altered-output control remains <code
      >CONDITIONAL</code
    >
    inside the Lab alone. Replay writes a new result directory and leaves the retained
    observation untouched. Timings and event IDs will differ.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .source-revision {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
